+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Ensure teardown cleanup is exhaustive and preserves every failure for callers
+after request and application context state has been safely released.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Exhaustive teardown execution
+Flask MUST invoke every registered request teardown callback, application-context
+teardown callback, and receiver of each corresponding teardown signal, even if
+one or more earlier teardown participants raise an exception. Flask MUST report
+the collected teardown failure or failures only after the applicable context
+has completed its cleanup and restored context-local state.
+
+#### Scenario: Request teardown has multiple failures
+- **WHEN** more than one request teardown participant raises while a request
+  context is popped
+- **THEN** all remaining request teardown participants run and the failures are
+  raised after cleanup finishes
+
+#### Scenario: Application-context teardown has multiple failures
+- **WHEN** more than one application-context teardown participant raises while
+  an application context is popped
+- **THEN** all remaining application-context teardown participants run,
+  context-local state is restored, and the failures are raised after cleanup
+  finishes
+
+### Requirement: Multiple teardown failure reporting
+On Python versions with exception-group support, Flask MUST raise all collected
+teardown failures together in an exception group. On older supported Python
+versions, Flask MUST raise the first collected teardown failure after running
+all teardown participants.
+
+#### Scenario: Exception-group-capable runtime
+- **WHEN** teardown collects multiple failures on a runtime that supports
+  exception groups
+- **THEN** the raised exception contains every collected teardown failure
